rate-directory synchronization; employee profile data is maintained in PostgreSQL (ASM-2)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid `googleIdentityToken` identifies an allowed Folio3 Google Workspace employee, with no bearer token on the session-creation operation.","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the response body contains every required `Session` field; a missing or malformed request returns status 400, and an unauthorized identity returns status 401 with an `ApiError` response.","when":"The client posts the token to `POST /auth/sessions`."},{"given":"The client has a valid authenticated session for an employee.","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body contains the authenticated employee's profile fields and registered vehicles; an unauthenticated request returns status 401 and an authenticated identity without permission returns status 403.","when":"The client requests `GET /me/profile`."},{"given":"The client has a valid authenticated employee session with registered vehicles.","id":"AC-REQ-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body contains a `vehicles` list of that employee's vehicles with the contract-defined fields; a request without authentication returns status 401.","when":"The client requests `GET /me/vehicles`."},{"given":"The client is authenticated and supplies a valid vehicle registration request containing a plate.","id":"AC-REQ-1.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle has an identifier, the submitted plate, and status `Active`; invalid input returns status 400, missing authentication returns status 401, and a conflicting registration returns status 409, each with the contract `ApiError` shape.","when":"The client posts to `POST /me/vehicles`."},{"given":"The client is authenticated and the office settings have their contract example defaults.","id":"AC-REQ-1.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body contains `officeTimezone` (`Asia/Karachi`), `releaseTime` (`08:00`), `schedulingWindowDays` (30), `workingDays`, and `holidaysAreWorkingDays`; a request without authentication returns status 401.","when":"The client requests `GET /parking/config`."},{"given":"The client has a valid authenticated session.","id":"AC-REQ-1.6","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body contains the office date and timezone, the employee's parking status, space status, release time, availability count, vehicle value, working days, and holiday setting; a request without authentication returns status 401.","when":"The client requests `GET /parking/today`."},{"given":"An authenticated dedicated parking holder has a reserved space today that has not already been released or claimed.","id":"AC-REQ-1.7","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the response body contains the release identifier, office date, `Released` status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt`; a non-holder receives status 403, a request without authentication receives status 401, and a conflicting state receives status 409.","when":"The holder posts to `POST /parking/releases/today`."},{"given":"An authenticated dedicated parking holder has saved releases, and optional `from` and `through` date filters are supplied where required by the scenario.","id":"AC-REQ-1.8","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body's `releases` list contains the holder's saved releases matching the requested date range; a request without authentication returns status 401 and a non-holder receives status 403.","when":"The holder requests `GET /parking/releases`."},{"given":"An authenticated dedicated parking holder submits one or more valid dates within the configured 30-day scheduling window.","id":"AC-REQ-1.9","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the response body's `releases` list contains the saved dates with their