-1.21","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body contains a verification identifier, office date and time, plate, verification, entry status, `greenActivationRequested`, and detail; invalid input returns status 400, and a verification-service failure returns status 503 with entry denied and an `ApiError` response.","when":"The integration posts to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`."},{"given":"The API is running with its published OpenAPI document enabled.","id":"AC-REQ-1.22","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response document lists all 21 contract paths and methods with the declared request, response, and security metadata.","when":"A client requests `GET /openapi/v1.json`."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"},{"lineEnd":15,"lineStart":8,"path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","quote":"security:\n  - oauth2:\n      - parking:access\npaths:\n  /auth/sessions:\n    post:\n      operationId: createSession\n      summary: Create a session from a Folio3 Google Workspace identity"}],"ears":"The API shall implement all 21 operations in `contracts/openapi.yaml` exactly as declared, including their paths, methods, security, parameters, request and response schemas, status codes, and examples, using HTTP API behavior only; this API build contains no mobile or web product screens.","id":"REQ-1","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An isolated PostgreSQL database is configured through `ConnectionStrings:App`, and the test creates its own employee, vehicle, and parking fixtures with `Seed:Demo=false`.","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"api","then":"The PostgreSQL database selected by `ConnectionStrings:App` contains a row for each persisted operation, and the returned vehicle, release, claim, verification, and settings values remain available after restart.","when":"The test registers a vehicle, schedules a release, claims an available space, records an entrance detection, updates office settings, restarts the API, and reads the corresponding records through the API and database."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":9,"lineStart":8,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\"App\")\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_1»\")));"},{"lineEnd":22,"lineStart":20,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();"},{"lineEnd":7,"lineStart":5,"path":"App.Api/AppDb.cs","quote":"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\n{\n}"}],"ears":"The API shall persist employee, vehicle, parking, entrance-verification, activity, and office-configuration records in PostgreSQL using the configured `ConnectionStrings:App` connection.","id":"REQ-2","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-2","ASM-2","ASM-7","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=false`.","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"api","then":"The row count for demo sample identifiers is 0.","when":"The API starts and its contract-backed tables are inspected for the identifiers used by demo sample records."},{"given":"A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=true`, with the contract examples available as seed sources.","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"api","then":"Each contract-backed table contains at least two sample rows using values from contract examples, and the second startup leaves the row count and existing row values unchanged.","when":"The API starts, then starts again against the same database."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":9,"lineStart":7,"path":"App.Api/SeedData.cs","quote":"public static void Run(AppDb db)\n    {\n    }"},{"lineEnd":7,"lineStart":5,"path":"App.Api/AppDb.cs","quote":"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\n{\n}"},{"lineEnd":24,"lineStart":22,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"db.Database.EnsureCreated();\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\"Seed:Demo\")) SeedData.Run(db);"}],"ears":"If `Seed:Demo` is true, then the API shall populate each contract-backed table with sample records using contract example values and insert records only when their contract-defined identifiers are absent; if it is false, startup leaves the database without demo inserts.","id":"REQ-3","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-3","I-4","ASM-9","ASM-10"]}],"suggestions":[]},{"assumptions":["The locked OpenAPI contract takes precedence over the conflicting email/password/reset default in ASM-1: session creation consumes `googleIdentityToken`, and protected operations use the contract's OAuth2 `parking:access` security.","ASM-3 maps standard users to `Employee`, administrator-only operations to `isParkingAdmin`, and release/claim eligibility to `assignedParkingStatus`.","ASM-7 stores administrator-managed office settings in PostgreSQL. The initial timezone and release time are `Asia/Karachi` and `08:00` as shown in contract examples; `schedulingWindowDays` is 30.","ASM-8 means dates and times use `Asia/Karachi` initially and the persisted office timezone after an administrator changes it.","Interpret “a few” as three records for each repeatable contract-backed data table and one record for a singleton office-settings table. Demo business fields follow contract examples, and dates are aligned to the current office date so default list operations return data.","ASM-9 means repeated demo seeding inserts records only when their contract-defined identifiers are absent and never overwrites or deletes existing records.","ASM-4 means the entrance camera/controller is an external caller; the API returns a decision and does not call or control physical entrance hardware.","ASM-5 and ASM-6 limit notification and reporting behavior to operations in the locked API contract; neither adds a notification delivery or scheduled report-email job. "],"nfrs":[],"outOfScope":["Physical camera/LPR operation and indicator-light actuation (ASM-4); the API accepts detection requests and returns verification decisions only.","Push and SMS notification delivery (ASM-5); no delivery operation is defined in the locked API contract.","Automated Monday report generation and email delivery (ASM-6); report data is exposed through `GET /admin/utilization`.","Custom report-builder functionality (ASM-6).","Email/password sign-in and reset-link flows from ASM-1 are superseded by the locked OpenAPI contract's Google identity token and OAuth2 security."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized Folio3 Google Workspace identity has a valid Google identity token.","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned session contains `accessToken`, `tokenType`, `expiresAt`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, and `isParkingAdmin`.","when":"The client sends that token as `googleIdentityToken` to `POST /auth/sessions`."},{"given":"The session request contains an invalid identity token or an identity that is not an allowed Folio3 Google Workspace identity.","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 and the returned error code is `unauthorized`.","when":"The client calls `POST /auth/sessions`."},{"given":"An employee is authenticated and has profile and vehicle records.","id":"AC-REQ-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned fields identify that employee and include their assigned parking status, assigned floor, and vehicles.","when":"The employee calls `GET /me/profile`."},{"given":"An employee is authenticated and has registered vehicles.","id":"AC-REQ-1.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned `vehicles` list contains that employee's vehicles and no other employee's vehicles.","when":"The employee calls `GET /me/vehicles`."},{"given":"An employee is authenticated and submits a valid plate with optional vehicle details.","id":"AC-REQ-1.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle has the submitted fields and `status` equal to `Active`.","when":"The employee calls `POST /me/vehicles`."},{"given":"An employee submits a vehicle request with a missing required plate or a plate already registered to that employee.","id":"AC-REQ-1.6","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 for invalid input or 409 for a conflict, and the returned error contains the contract error fields.","when":"The employee calls `POST /me/vehicles`."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /auth/sessions`, `GET /me/profile`, and `GET` and `POST /me/vehicles` with the request schemas, response schemas, security, and status codes declared in the locked OpenAPI contract.","id":"REQ-1","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1"],"stability":0.82},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The office has not changed its initial parking configuration.","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned fields show `officeTime